    {
      "type": "text",
      "headline": {
        "text": "Washington's June limits left an opening",
        "facts": [
          "B1"
        ]
      },
      "body": {
        "text": "In June the Trump administration put temporary limits on distributing OpenAI and Anthropic models over cyberattack concerns. WIRED says that created an opening for Mistral, which pitches open weights as a hedge.",
        "facts": [
          "B1",
          "F10"
        ]
      },
      "quote_id": null,
      "quote_excerpt": null,
      "number_ids": [],
      "image": {
        "kind": "none",
        "value": ""
      },
      "spread_with_next": false
    },
    {
      "type": "landing",
      "headline": {
        "text": "Still unanswered",
        "facts": [
          "F2",
          "N9"
        ]
      },
      "body": {
        "text": "Mistral says weights land by end of October. Full independent benchmarks are pending, and hardware needs, API pricing and license terms have not been given.",
        "facts": [
          "F2",
          "N9",
          "F4"
        ]
      },
      "quote_id": null,
      "quote_excerpt": null,
      "number_ids": [],
      "image": {
        "kind": "none",
        "value": ""
      },
      "spread_with_next": false
    }
  ],
  "follow": "Follow Helios to see whether the weights land by the end of October and whether independent benchmarks back Mistral's claims.",
  "caption": {
    "text": "French AI lab Mistral launched a public preview of Mistral Large 4, nicknamed Le Chonk, on Oct 6. Mistral says the 1-trillion-parameter model is the strongest open-weight model made outside China. Open-weight means the trained parameters are released so anyone can modify and self-host the model. Mistral says those weights arrive by the end of October.\n\nEarly testing by Artificial Analysis, reported by The Register, places the preview well behind OpenAI and Anthropic flagships but well ahead of the top US open-weight model, Thinking Machines Lab's Inkling. Mistral's cybersecurity scores are its own and were not independently confirmed. Mistral also says this is the first milestone funded by its €3 billion Series D, raised in September.\n\nWould you rather build on a model you can host yourself, or a closed one from a big lab?\n\nFollow Helios to see whether the weights actually arrive by the end of October.",
    "facts": [
      "F1",
      "F2",
      "F3",
      "F4",
      "F5",
      "F7",
      "F9",
      "N5",
      "N9",
      "B1"
    ]
  },
  "edit_notes": [
    "Cover 1 leads with Mistral because well_known is true; says 'says' to keep the F4 attribution.",
    "Slide 2 includes TechCrunch's note that the model is not open-weight yet, so the preview/weights gap is shown rather than hidden.",
    "Used 'substantial margin' unquoted as paraphrase; it is not a QUOTES entry.",
    "Independent testing (F5) is single-source (The Register), so it is attributed on the slide.",
    "Cyber figures (N6, N7) are shown as Mistral's claims with the not-verified note; split stat body carries the hedge.",
    "GPU count (3,800 vs 4,000) left out because sources disagree and it adds little.",
    "Series D funding figures differ across outlets, so only the euro amount appears, in the caption only.",
    "No quote slide: all quotes are single-source, and the story had enough material without one.",
    "One background slide (B1, single source WIRED, attributed). B2 left out as off-center.",
    "Landing slide lists NOT ANSWERED items, no invented suspense."
  ]
}

