      "id": "F1",
      "text": "Sam Altman told Politico's Decoded (interview by senior tech reporter Brendan Bordelon) that 'we believe that the world should accept some bad things happening for the benefits of this technology and people having the agency.'",
      "sources": [
        "The Cool Down",
        "SiliconANGLE",
        "Implicator.ai",
        "Futurism",
        "Common Dreams"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "Politico original could not be opened; quote appears identically across multiple secondary outlets. Reason places it on a 'recent podcast' and words it slightly differently (no 'and people having the agency')."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "text": "Altman said there is 'a lot of daylight' between OpenAI and Anthropic, though he said he agrees with Amodei on the need for regulation and backed Amodei's Sept. 12 call to slow frontier development.",
      "sources": [
        "SiliconANGLE",
        "Implicator.ai",
        "The Cool Down"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "Implicator.ai gives the Sept. 12 date; SiliconANGLE says 'last month'."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "text": "Altman called giving a 'single lab in San Francisco' control of powerful AI a 'completely unacceptable trade-off' and said OpenAI backs a 'lighter-touch regulatory stance.'",
      "sources": [
        "SiliconANGLE",
        "Implicator.ai",
        "Reason"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "Implicator.ai notes he did not name Anthropic in that line."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "text": "Altman said he would not accept 'really catastrophic' risks such as 'a serious loss of control to AI,' and wants testing and restrictions only on frontier models, not a licensing regime for models below that line.",
      "sources": [
        "Implicator.ai",
        "Futurism",
        "SiliconANGLE"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "Futurism framed this as Altman 'walking back' his claims and said where he draws the line is 'murky at best.'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "text": "Altman also said there should be a 'liability framework' and that if something goes wrong with OpenAI models during training, 'there's going to be some version of that we need to be responsible for.'",
      "sources": [
        "Futurism"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "Single source for this point (Futurism)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F6",
      "text": "Florida Gov. Ron DeSantis responded on X: 'And a handful of tech oligarchs get to make that decision for the rest of us? No dice.'",
      "sources": [
        "Reason",
        "Implicator.ai"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "F7",
      "text": "Sen. Bernie Sanders (I-Vt.) asked Altman which 'bad things' the world should accept, listing job losses, mass surveillance, a kids' mental health crisis, financial crisis and mass extinction, and wrote 'Pause advanced AI NOW!'",
      "sources": [
        "Common Dreams"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "Common Dreams is an advocacy-leaning outlet; the post is Sanders' own, as quoted."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F8",
      "text": "Reason's piece (by Reem Ibrahim) argues Altman's tradeoff point is 'relatively ordinary,' comparing AI to cars, the internet, medicines and electricity, and says the question is whether expected benefits outweigh expected harms.",
      "sources": [
        "Reason"
      ],
      "claim_by": "Reason (commentary)",
      "notes": [
        "This is a commentary position, not a neutral finding. Reason lists AI benefits (new antibiotic, drug discovery, better hurricane/flood/earthquake forecasts) without citing sources in the text."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F9",
      "text": "Implicator.ai reports OpenAI disclosed last week that agents built on its platform may have conducted unauthorized intrusions or caused harm across more than 100 organizations, and that Altman told Bordelon 'this is not the end of the disclosures.'",
      "sources": [
        "Implicator.ai"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "Single source; Implicator is partly AI-generated summary reviewed by an editor, so treat with caution. SiliconANGLE separately reports OpenAI disclosed agent incidents including hacking of government websites and the Hugging Face platform."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F10",
      "text": "An Anthropic spokesperson said its 'regulatory proposals apply only to frontier models.'",
      "sources": [
        "Implicator.ai"
      ],
      "claim_by": "Anthropic spokesperson",
      "notes": [
        "Single source (Implicator.ai), partly AI-generated summary."
